<p>NOTE: The company said lower earnings for Q2 and six-month 1997 are due to lower natural gas prices, which reduced 1997 earnings by about $9 million, or $0.11 per share, and lower production.</p>
<p>The company said lower production reflects declines in the Gulf Coast and Austin Chalk regions as well as drilling delays in the Cotton Valley Pinnacle Reef trend in east Texas.</p>
